Virtual Environment 

    .private workspace for Python project 
    .allows package installation without affecting the whole computer 
    .it contains:
        .private Python interpreter
        .private site-packages folder
        .its own pip
        .its own installed libraries
        .activation strips 


Without venv:
    .installing Django for one project installs it for every project
    .different projects might need different versions of the same package
    .the system Python gets messy and breaks things
    .deployments become unpredictable
    .debugging becomes painful

With it:
    .each project has its own Django, its own Click, and own DB driver
    .no version conflicts
    .whole environment can be deleted safely
    .reproducibility becomes easy


Need for it:
    .building Django apps
    .creating CLI tools 
    .installing Click
    .using SQL drivers
    .running multiple Python projects


venv folder:
    .Python interpreter
    .pip
    .site packages
    .activation scripts

